# Append-only logs (looper#53): a local `git merge` keeps both sides' new lines
# instead of conflicting. GitHub's own mergeability check ignores custom merge
# drivers, so new entries go in one file per PR under docs/learnings/ and
# .SEED/decisions/ — that is the real fix; this is the safety net.
docs/LEARNINGS.md merge=union
.SEED/decisions.md merge=union
.SEED/gotchas.md merge=union
